id: pm-linear-atomic-replay-revision
title: Revalidate current target revisions before recovering an atomic Linear import
description: "Read-only synthetic scratch probe during field ownership work: atomic import commits input A; a peer then changes the target title through the SDK; replaying A uses the same transaction id and reports recovered while current SDK state still differs from A. Existing content-keyed recovery is not a current-state acknowledgement. This is inherited import behavior and is not changed by the observational preview."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: replay,revision,sync
created_at: "2026-10-27T09:45:22.258Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:51:27.414Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Bind import retry decisions to current SDK target revisions; revalidate every expected revision before recovery; decide unchanged through current target reads; preserve peer edits or surface a typed refusal; seeded model tests cover older-input replays and interleavings without git.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T09:51:27.414Z",codex-agent,"Synthetic non-git probe: sameTransaction=true, replayReportedRecovered=true, currentTargetStillDiffersFromInput=true. Reproducer: node test/ownership-inherited-replay.ts. Existing target was edited through PmClient.update before replay; no hosted provider was contacted. Ownership previews separately read current SDK state and do not apply or recover imports."
files[2]{path,scope}:
